## Security Audit: UAF/Double-Free/Overflow (2026-09-04)
### Vulnerabilities Found and Fixed:
- [CRITICAL] UAF in ky_vm_load_string: kyx_lexer_destroy(lx) called before kyx_lexer_has_error(lx) read - saved error state before destroy
- [MEDIUM] Out-of-bounds read in call_proto: while condition `pc+3 < code_count` could read 1 byte past end - fixed to `pc+4 <= code_count`
- [MEDIUM] Missing bounds check on proto->strings[B/C] access in 5 locations (OP_GETGLOBAL x2, OP_GETFIELD, OP_SETGLOBAL, OP_NATIVECALL)
- [LOW] Dead code: vm->strings array allocated but never populated, string_count always 0 - removed dead free loop
### Files Unaffected (safe):
- physics.c: all array accesses bounded by max counts with overflow guards
- hashmap.c/array.c/string.c: no UAF/double-free issues found
- memory.c: standard malloc/free wrappers, safe

